              "details": "Next.js App Router applications that pass binary arguments (such as Uint8Array or Blob values) to functions using the `use cache` directive can produce identical cache keys for distinct arguments, allowing cached results to be shared across users — cross-user disclosure of cached data or cache poisoning. This affects applications using `use cache` with binary arguments.",
